WEBVTT
NOTE SYNC_TYPE: HUMAN_VERIFIED
NOTE Track: 1-07 - The Penumbra
NOTE Artist: The Stardust Engine
NOTE Album: Sanctuary (Zero-G) (2003)

00:00:10.850 --> 00:00:19.776
As our trajectory continues, the massive body of the parent planet moves directly between us and the sun.

00:00:23.119 --> 00:00:32.445
We are now entering the penumbra—the outer edge of the celestial shadow.

00:00:32.485 --> 00:00:36.168
The temperature will begin to drop rapidly as the light is obscured.

00:00:39.090 --> 00:00:43.498
Solar efficiency will fall to critical levels.

00:00:45.279 --> 00:00:55.185
Prepare for deep space isolation as we cross the threshold into total darkness.

00:00:55.185 --> 00:01:24.904
[Instrumental Intro — Mechanical Drum Machine, Distorted Fretless Bass & Icy Analog Synths]

00:01:24.904 --> 00:01:28.467
The edge of the planet is cutting the light

00:01:32.311 --> 00:01:36.335
A massive eclipse in the middle of the night

00:01:39.818 --> 00:01:43.400
The temperature drops on the console screen

00:01:43.499 --> 00:01:47.700
The coldest shadow that I've ever seen

00:01:47.900 --> 00:01:52.641
The solar arrays are starting to freeze

00:01:52.741 --> 00:01:56.800
A sudden drop by a hundred degrees

00:01:56.800 --> 00:02:00.200
Entering the shadow, crossing the line

00:02:00.200 --> 00:02:02.423
Losing the light, losing the sign

00:02:02.563 --> 00:02:06.384
The power is draining, the cabin is dark

00:02:06.504 --> 00:02:11.500
Waiting in the black for a single spark

00:02:11.500 --> 00:02:16.147
Caught in the penumbra, cold and blind

00:02:16.167 --> 00:02:20.208
Leaving the warmth of the sun behind

00:02:20.288 --> 00:02:23.869
A temporary death in the deep space freeze

00:02:23.969 --> 00:02:28.500
Drifting completely on the dark space breeze

00:02:28.500 --> 00:02:31.300
Hold your breath and wait for the dawn

00:02:31.330 --> 00:02:37.292
Caught in the penumbra until the night is gone

00:02:43.755 --> 00:02:48.219
The machinery hums with a desperate sound

00:02:48.340 --> 00:02:52.043
A million miles from the solid ground

00:02:52.203 --> 00:02:56.387
The silence out here has a sharper edge

00:02:56.588 --> 00:03:00.500
Like standing alone on an icy ledge

00:03:00.500 --> 00:03:03.200
I close my eyes in the pitch-black room

00:03:03.200 --> 00:03:05.713
Swallowed alive by the planetary tomb

00:03:06.193 --> 00:03:10.395
Entering the shadow, crossing the line

00:03:10.435 --> 00:03:14.376
Losing the light, losing the sign

00:03:14.516 --> 00:03:18.558
The power is draining, the cabin is dark

00:03:18.658 --> 00:03:23.800
Waiting in the black for a single spark

00:03:23.800 --> 00:03:28.583
Caught in the penumbra, cold and blind

00:03:28.764 --> 00:03:32.486
Leaving the warmth of the sun behind

00:03:32.886 --> 00:03:36.148
A temporary death in the deep space freeze

00:03:36.368 --> 00:03:40.200
Drifting completely on the dark space breeze

00:03:40.200 --> 00:03:44.112
Hold your breath and wait for the dawn

00:03:44.172 --> 00:03:48.875
Caught in the penumbra until the night is gone

00:03:48.875 --> 00:04:18.363
[Synthesizer Solo — Dissonant Analog Synthesizer Over Mechanical Drums]

00:04:18.363 --> 00:04:21.500
Just a phase of the orbit.

00:04:21.500 --> 00:04:25.000
Just a test of the steel.

00:04:25.000 --> 00:04:28.500
The shadow is heavy.

00:04:28.500 --> 00:04:31.500
But the math is real.

00:04:33.518 --> 00:04:36.000
Wait for the transit...

00:04:37.202 --> 00:04:41.500
Wait for the light...

00:04:41.500 --> 00:04:47.493
Caught in the penumbra, cold and blind

00:04:47.693 --> 00:04:51.393
